    "created_at": "2026-06-09T16:31:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-09T16:31:51Z",
    "body": "What's the motivation behind privacy-preserving rendering of subtitles and captions not taking into account user preferences? As I understand it, WebVTT rendering done by the UA or OS is already supposed to be privacy-preserving, and the current design choice is that there are no Web APIs for querying user preferences or for extracting styling choices from the rendered captions.\r\n\r\nIt seems odd that privacy-preservation should have a negative impact on accessibility settings that aren't exposed to pages.\r\n\r\n(aside: I actually don't think the argument for prohibiting Web APIs for accessing user settings holds up any more, but that's a whole different discussion)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
